<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield climbs to 13.82 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield climbs to 13.82 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills edged up to 13.82 percent at an auction on Tuesday from 13.56 percent at the last auction on July 22, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   July 29	    July 22</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K3010974     KZ43K2310979</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,639		1,283</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 600		  501</p>
<p> Average price			 96.66 pct	  96.72</p>
<p> Average yield			 13.82 pct	  13.56</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Oct 30, 1997     Oct 23, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
